The constraint check shows 6 Larch Grove is not in a conservation area, is not a listed building, and has no tree preservation order. That helps, but whether your garden room needs an application depends on its size and position.

The council's outbuilding guidance says that garden rooms and sheds usually don't need an application if they meet all of these conditions:

- **Height:** under 2.5 metres
- **Position:** behind the front wall of the house
- **Coverage:** less than half the garden area

If your plans meet all three, you probably won't need an application. If any one doesn't, you likely will. I can't give a formal planning opinion, so if you're unsure, or if the building is close to a boundary or is larger than the guidance allows, submit a formal application or ask the council for confirmation before you start.

If you tell me the planned height, where it will sit relative to the house's front wall, and roughly what share of the garden it will cover, I can give you a clearer picture of whether it fits the usual exemption.
